From 34ab44d0e2add61680eae58e5a5a2b833ca2e8e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 11/16] serial: KNC console over I2C (i2c-pxa, SC16IS7xx on
 8250, hvc)

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6:
 - i2c-pxa: the KNC SBOX-wired PXA I2C controller (self-wiring, no
   platform clocks), with the gate that lets the RAS module take over
   the bus temporarily, and the locally carried slave client header.
 - 8250_sc16is7xx: an SC16IS7xx UART behind that I2C bus as an 8250
   port, used as the serial console (ttyS0).
 - HVC_MIC: the hvc console over the host (hvc0).

Adaptations for 6.18:
 - i2c-pxa: i2c_new_client_device, probe without id, the slave header
   carried locally since 5.9 merged it into platform_data; bus-wedge
   messages rate limited.
 - 8250_sc16is7xx: serial8250_register_8250_port; the 8250 core calls
   serial_in/out with the port lock held, so i2c_transfer() may only
   trylock the adapter: -EAGAIN is retried for up to 5 ms, real errors
   are not, and a failed read returns harmless IIR/LSR stand-ins (a
   lost IER write froze tty TX for good). Since 4.2 the adapter lock
   may not be taken from irq context: master_xfer() is driven under a
   private spinlock. The chip is instantiated at 0x4D and 0x48; the
   probe checks the scratch register and skips the empty address.
   uart_port.timeout is gone (6.1). 6.17's set_io_from_upio() warns on
   the private iotype: skipped.
 - Kconfig/Makefile against the upstream sc16is7xx i2c/spi split.
 - The KDB console hook in the driver is dropped with KDB.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
